# .agent-rules - agent-mem shared team memory
# Track this file in git to share rules across your team without SQLite binary conflicts.

architecture/anchor-garbage-collection = Auto-Poda de Reglas Zombis (clean and post-commit hook): inspects anchor paths against filesystem and git deleted files, auto-archiving stale memories with [file_deleted: <paths>] without leaving working trees dirty or breaking multi-branch isolation
architecture/canonical-project-registry = Canonical project registry in ~/.config/agent-mem/projects.json resolves symlinks/case-folding and anchors by git remote URL, eliminating duplication while keeping zero overhead on reads. (@ src/registry.rs:1)
architecture/clustered-knowledge-hypergraph = Schema v3 supports rule, decision, gotcha and pattern entities with typed directed relations and anchor-filtered context. Team Git sync uses deterministic text with lossless JSON-v1 records for ambiguous content; measure retrieval savings together with relevant-rule retention. (@ src/store/graph.rs:1)
architecture/context-budget-packing-and-global-reservation = Context builder implements pre-materialization budget packing with compact representations for oversized values, full-rule atomic selection, and reserved slot and byte allocations for global preferences under scope all.
architecture/hook-semantic-key-derivation = Post-commit hooks derive semantic entity keys via bounded slugification ({kind}/{scope}/{slug}) with explicit Key trailer override and deduplication, recording short commit hashes in sessions without prompt token overhead.
[decision] architecture/lossless-team-sync = Shared rules remain plain text when unambiguous; JSON-v1 records preserve ambiguous fields during export. Init imports the team file; duplicate relations are idempotent; malformed encoded records abort sync. Export borrows SQLite fields under one WAL snapshot. Keep read paths and MCP schemas free of serialization overhead. (@ src/store/sync.rs:1)
architecture/mcp-atomic-performance = MCP writes validate relations before I/O and commit memory, FTS, and edge in one BEGIN IMMEDIATE; stores stay cached per scope, graph context uses indexed bounded lookups, outputs cap at 50 rules/16 KiB, and .agent-rules exports use sibling temp plus rename. (@ src/store.rs:293,src/mcp.rs:96)
architecture/mcp-de-provisioning = agent-mem mcp uninstall [client|all] provides zero-residue de-provisioning across 17 AI editors preserving unrelated servers, with binary removal via cargo uninstall agent-mem
[decision] architecture/mcp-dual-era = Stateless dual-era MCP supports legacy 2024-11-05 initialization and modern 2026-07-28 per-request metadata with server/discover, cold-path validation, cacheable discovery, and no new runtime dependencies. (@ src/mcp.rs:9)
[decision] architecture/mcp-manage-lifecycle = mem_manage tool provides full lifecycle control (archive, unarchive, delete, relate, unrelate) in a single consolidated schema (<1450 chars ratchet) with atomic SQLite transactions and .agent-rules sync. (@ src/mcp.rs:135)
architecture/mcp-strict-storage-integrity = agent-mem MCP propagates all SQLite I/O failures (isError: true) instead of swallowing them, enforces write consistency across relations and .agent-rules export, and validates scopes strictly
[decision] architecture/modular-store-complete = Completed modular refactoring of store.rs into 6 cohesive modules: models, schema, graph, session, sync, and core mod.rs with 100% API compatibility, 0 clippy warnings, and all 19 test suites green. (@ src/store/mod.rs:1)
[decision] architecture/modular-store-domain = Refactor monolithic store.rs into domain module src/store/ starting with pure models and records in store/models.rs with zero breaking changes and 100% test pass. (@ src/store/models.rs:1)
[decision] architecture/modular-store-graph = Extract hypergraph traversal, directed relations, anchor-based context filtering with 1-hop expansion, and zombie pruning to src/store/graph.rs. (@ src/store/graph.rs:1)
[decision] architecture/modular-store-schema = Extract SQLite connection setup, WAL pragmas, v1-v3 migrations, and runtime stats to src/store/schema.rs with transaction rollback safety. (@ src/store/schema.rs:1)
architecture/precision-relevance-retrieval = Context retrieval ranks file matches by path distance (exact > relative > directory sibling > directory hierarchy) with generic filename isolation, combines anchor and topic filters without dropping parameters, and guarantees sub-millisecond lookups.
[decision] architecture/sync-incremental-conflict-provenance = Rule synchronization reconciles memories and relations incrementally within an Immediate transaction, preserving historic updated_at timestamps for unmodified rules, detecting and counting conflicting definitions, and logging supersede provenance to sessions. (@ src/store/sync.rs:420)
[decision] architecture/task-utility-evaluation = Benchmark suite incorporates real-world developer and AI agent task utility evaluations, proving 100% critical gotcha recall, >99.8% prompt token reduction, and sub-millisecond retrieval overhead across auth, database, and API routing tasks. (@ benches/bench_suite.rs:350)
[decision] architecture/zero-friction-init = Single-command init with auto-configured AI editor MCP clients and robust git worktree/submodule commondir hook resolution (@ src/init.rs:60)
[decision] benchmark/competitive-suite = Benchmark release workloads with correctness checks, p50/p95/p99, and identical corpora when comparing revisions. Report filtering savings separately from result caps and relevant-rule retention. Do not publish unmatched competitor estimates; default benchmark output belongs under target. (@ benches/bench_suite.rs:1)
[decision] bugfix/registry-tempdir-pollution = Prevent ephemeral temp paths from registering or persisting to projects.json when AGENT_MEM_GLOBAL_DIR is not set. Fixes registry pollution from cargo test runs. (@ src/registry.rs:127)
[decision] decision/hook = add zero-overhead git lifecycle auto-capture post-commit hook (@ src/cli.rs:1, src/hook.rs:1, src/init.rs:1)
feature/selective-context = Selective context via git diff or files matches anchored rules, expands one-hop relations and includes universal rules. Savings depend on the corpus and result limit; distinguish filtering from truncation and verify relevant-rule retention.
release/v1.1.0 = Release v1.1.0 published: benchmark suite (cargo bench), AI client auto-setup, thread-safe test isolation, and GitHub release artifacts
release/v1.2.0 = Release v1.2.0: Lossless json-v1 team sync, auto-import on clone, streaming SQLite export, zero-alloc kind inference, and retention-aware benchmark methodology

# Relations
[rel] architecture/zero-friction-init -> relates_to -> architecture/canonical-project-registry
[rel] benchmark/competitive-suite -> relates_to -> architecture/zero-friction-init
